	(text "U5 TPS259631DDAR eFuse (PROPOSED; TPS2596 SLVSET8A p.4, p.22):\nIN = VBUS, OUT = +5V. R35 357k / R36 43.2k / R37 100k set UVLO and OVLO,\nR38 1.21k sets ILM, C32 47 nF sets dVdt, C33 4.7 uF on VBUS.\nFLT open-drain (TP4); R39 pull-up DNP. Not simulated or measured."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 20 18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "118c4da0-4f66-4010-a3dd-25b73927fbe1")
	)
	(text "Design intent (Rev A, revision 4; nothing here is simulated or measured; details and citations in\n    docs/schematic/power.md)\nPROPOSED  +5V (U5 OUT) entry: C1 10 uF + C2 100 nF.\nPROPOSED  U1 TPS79901: VOUT = 1.193 V x (1 + R1/R2) = 3.316 V nominal (R1 17.8k, R2 10.0k). CFB 1 nF\n    (see note).\nVERIFIED  TPS79901 CFB is required for stability; 3 pF to 1 nF when R1||R2 = 250k; <5 pF for fast\n    start (SBVS056L p.14, 8.2.2.6).\nUNRESOLVED  Here R1||R2 = 6.4k, not 250k: the datasheet range was not stated for this impedance; 1\n    nF is a PROPOSED value.\nPROPOSED  3V3 load estimate (rev 2): OPA857 26.8 mA max + OPA855 19.5 mA max (IQ 17.8 typ, 16-19.5\n    mA at VS = 5 V, OPA855 SBOS622D PDF p.7; Fig 6-27 p.12 shows about 16-17.5 mA at 3.3 V, so 19.5\n    is conservative) + TLV3605 17.5 mA max + OPA2320 ~2 mA = about 66 mA. U1 TPS79901 is rated 200\n    mA. PROPOSED, not measured.\nREMOVED  (decision 12) U2 LM27762 +/-3V7, 5V_A bead/caps, PGOOD_VGA and TP1: the VCA821 VGA is gone,\n    the OPA855 runs from 3V3.\nPROPOSED  U3 LT8365 values per docs/calculations/apd-bias-design.md sections 3.2 and 4: 500 kHz (RT\n    84.5k), L1 10 uH, boost to ~110 V + doubler.\nVERIFIED  SYNC/MODE: float = pulse-skip, GND = Burst, 100k to GND = Burst/SSFM (LT8365 Rev. A p.7).\n    BIAS tie to GND if unused; INTVCC 1 uF (p.7).\nPROPOSED  EN/UVLO 200k/200k from 5V_HVIN, always connected. Q3 DMN2056U-7 pulls EN/UVLO to GND = HV\n    OFF. Gate = HV_DIS, R33 100k pull-up to 3V3_D, R34 1k series: HV is OFF until the ESP32 drives\n    HV_DIS low after verifying the DAC (decision 11). J1 HV FORCE ON (DNP) shorts the gate to GND\n    for bench use without firmware.\nPROPOSED  U4 TPS7A2033 3V3_D: 300 mA, radio must stay disabled; load est. 60 mA\n    (docs/research/module-controller.md). CIN 1 uF, COUT 10 uF + 1 uF (datasheet minimum 1 uF, max\n    200 uF: SBVS338H p.5).\nPROPOSED  BIAS: R28 0R to GND fitted; R29 0R to 5V_HVIN DNP. Fit exactly one of them. SYNC options\n    R26/R27/TP2 are DNP.\nPROPOSED  D2 (GND to SW, from the p.30 250 V example, purpose not stated) is DNP. Q1/Q2 clamp ~150\n    uA. C8 and R19 form filter stage 1.\nPROPOSED  HV_MON = HV_OUT/101 (R20+R32 10M, R21 100k): 1.39 V at 140 V. Stage 2 filter (10k + 10 nF)\n    is on the front-end sheet.\nNet names: HV_V1, HV_PUMP, HV_RAW, HV_OUT, HV_CLAMP, 5V_HVIN, EN, SYNC, BIAS, RT, SS, VC, FBX are\n    local labels; APD_BIAS = HV_FILT.\nHierarchical pins: in VBUS, DAC_HV, HV_DIS; out 3V3, 3V3_D, APD_BIAS, HV_MON.\nPROPOSED  (decision 14, revision 4) U5 TPS259631DDAR eFuse: IN pin 4 = VBUS (single 5 V input from\n    the Connector sheet), OUT pin 5 = +5V (internal rail for U1, U3 via L2, U4), GND pin 1 and\n    exposed pad pin 9 = GND (TPS2596 SLVSET8A p.4). Fixed-clamp variants rejected; this variant\n    gives x1 auto-retry (Device Comparison p.3). Abs max on IN 21 V (p.1, p.5).\nPROPOSED  UVLO/OVLO divider R35 357k / R36 43.2k / R37 100k (1 %): overvoltage cut-off 5.76-6.20 V\n    rising (below the 7.0 V abs max of the TPS79901, SBVS056L p.4), UVLO 4.06-4.32 V rising,\n    3.72-4.00 V falling (calculated with tolerances, not simulated).\nPROPOSED  ILM R38 1.21k 1 %: ILIM 0.68 / 0.76 / 0.84 A min/typ/max (TPS2596 Eq. 5 p.22). A real\n    current limit, not the 0.5 A USB budget. TP3 IMON on ILM (about 0.79 V/A). C32 47 nF on dVdt:\n    about 5.3 ms ramp, about 23 mA inrush into an assumed 25 uF (estimate, measure in G1).\nPROPOSED  FLT (pin 6) open-drain, TP4; R39 100k pull-up DNP to 3V3_D. UNRESOLVED: both rails are off\n    while the eFuse is cut off, so a pull-up reads 0 V and cannot separate fault from no power; FLT\n    is not routed to the ESP32. FLT pin abs max not read.\nPROPOSED  C33 4.7 uF 25 V 0805 on VBUS at IN. C1/C2 stay on +5V (OUT). Removed: TPS2121, +5V_CABLE,\n    PWR_SRC, old R39-R42, C34, the PR1 divider.\nPROPOSED  Budget about 0.19 A worst case from +5V (docs/research/usb-standalone-power.md section\n    1.5, estimate) plus up to 35 mA on 3V3 for the LVDS fan-out U50 (LVDS104 p.5); radio must stay\n    disabled. UNRESOLVED: whether a bus-powered hub holds a module to 100 mA.\nPROPOSED  ERC: U5 OUT (pin 5) is power_out on the +5V net, so +5V needs no PWR_FLAG; the root\n    PWR_FLAG #FLG04 sits on VBUS. USB-alone firmware starts HV at the low-bias end in steps\n    (PROPOSED)."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 308 28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4 1.4)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5715bd95-1c8a-4ae9-895c-582a454f6510")
	)
	(text "3V3_D: U4 TPS7A2033 3.3 V, 300 mA, own rail\nfor ESP32-C6, CAN, DAC, ADC (about 60 mA est.).\nESP32 radio MUST stay disabled (Wi-Fi TX peaks\n251-382 mA). PROPOSED, estimate not measured."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 172 50 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "badbae25-d47c-4455-9b30-ffc47ac75991")
	)
	(text "Power: VBUS in -> U5 eFuse -> +5V. U1 TPS79901 3V3, U4 TPS7A2033 3V3_D, U3 LT8365 APD bias (100-220 V) -> APD_BIAS."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 20 12.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d35a803b-0929-4900-924f-5c965612a28c")
	)
	(text "HV WARNING\nAPD bias reaches 220 V. Stored energy ~2.3 mJ (docs/calculations/apd-bias-design.md section 4). Can\n    be hazardous.\nNever probe HV_OUT, HV_RAW, HV_PUMP, HV_V1 or HV_CLAMP directly. Use HV_MON (HV_OUT/101) for\n    observation.\nCapacitors C5-C8, C25 and resistors R19, R30 carry >= 200 V ratings; keep 200 V creepage/clearance\n    on every HV_ net,\nseries-limited, with the HV netclass 1.0 mm clearance. Keep the APD_BIAS/FBX area away from TIA_IN.\nHV is OFF by default (Q3 gate pulled up); J1 FORCE ON overrides the firmware disable: fit only on\n    the bench with the DAC set. Discharge through the divider takes ~0.5 s: wait before touching.\nReferences: LT8365 Rev. A datasheet p.30 (250 V example), DC2838A demo manual Rev. 0."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 308 190 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4 1.4)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e4636cc8-7880-46b0-86cf-8f0cb2e00939")
	)
